## Goal

`cargo jackioh gate --duos` plays two matchups over the same game count:

- the Easy AI team against the random-policy team, unchanged;
- the Easy AI team against a team whose seats each play the 1v1 greedy baseline (`greedy_action`) in their own duel and never pass.

The greedy matchup has its own floor, `DUOS_GATE_GREEDY_WIN_FLOOR = 0.7` in `crates/ai/src/config.rs`, set from measured runs. Two daily tests show a weakened pass heuristic clearing the random floor and failing the greedy one. The heuristic passes the first passable card each round, before anything else.

**Planner's measurements.** This design was built in a scratch copy. Every run had 0 refused actions, 0 fallbacks and 0 search panics.

| series, games | shipping vs random | shipping vs greedy | weakened vs random | weakened vs greedy |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `duos-tune` 1–200 (fresh deals) | 200/200 | 168/200 | 200/200 | 76/200 |
| `duos-gate:v1` 1–20 (the CLI's) | 20/20 | 16/20 | 20/20 | 9/20 |
| `gate` 1–20 (the daily tests') | 20/20 | 19/20 | 20/20 | 7/20 |

Binomial(20, 0.84) puts P(≤13) at 0.03, so 14 of 20 is what this AI reaches in 95% of runs (§9.9's rule): the floor is 0.7.

